DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250630T004636Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250920T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250922T150000
SUMMARY:Monthly Campout:  Davis Mountains & Balmorhea
DESCRIPTION:Monthly Campout: Davis Mountains State Park (Star Party) &amp; Balmorhea State Park (Swimming)\nWe are firming up the details for our September campout\, which will be at Fort Davis\, Saturday - Monday\, September 20-22. There is no school on Monday\, September 22\, so we are taking advantage of the long weekend. This is a heads up for anyone who needs to put in for the time off work. This is going to be a unique campout that we have not ever done before. We will see an amazing part of West Texas and attend a Star Party at McDonald Observatory for the Astronomy Merit Badge. Scouts must have passed the swim test in the past year in order to swim. Scouts and adults should bring swimsuits\, towels\, masks\, etc. This campout is capped at 32 people by first to register.\n\nCampout Itinerary:\n\nLocation:\nSaturday\, September 20:\nArrive at LTMS at 7:00 am\nDepart LTMS by 7:30 am\nMap: https://maps.app.goo.gl/uCgHS5iFQETSEH9V7\nArrive at Davis Mountains SP at 1:30 pm\nScouts should pack a sack lunch for the road!\nCampsites 49-52 at Davis Mountains State Park\nPark Map:\nhttps://tpwd.texas.gov/publications/pwdpubs/media/park_maps/pwd_mp_p4501_004d.pdf\n\nSunday\, September 21:\nBalmorhea State Park\nMap: https://maps.app.goo.gl/QjmNfqSUmKjfcE5x7\nCampsites #14\, #15\, #17 &amp; #20 (group site)\nPark Map:\nhttps://tpwd.texas.gov/publications/pwdpubs/media/park_maps/pwd_mp_p4501_002h.pdf\n\nActivity Schedule:\nSaturday:\nArrive approximately 1:30 pm\nSet up camp\nDinner - Patrol Cooking\, James and Mike Bat grubmasters\nAstronomy MB - prep for the evening\nAll scouts should print and bring the MB worksheet:\nhttp://usscouts.org/usscouts/mb/mb022.asp\n\nHere is a link to the Astronomy MB pamphlet at the bottom of this page (no need to print):\nhttps://www.scouting.org/merit-badges/astronomy/\n\nStar Party at McDonald Observatory:\nhttps://mcdonaldobservatory.org/visitors\n20 minute drive:\nhttps://maps.app.goo.gl/VjBKzNJv6x4K5KH78\nLate night for all since Star Party begins at 8:45 pm\, arrive by 8:30 pm\nReturn to campsite\n\nSunday:\nBreakfast at Davis Mountains State Park\nOptional early morning trail hike. Trail Map:\nhttps://tpwd.texas.gov/publications/pwdpubs/media/park_maps/pwd_mp_p4501_0004f.pdf\nPack up camp\nMove to Balmorhea State Park (30 minute drive)\nSet up camp\nLunch - patrol cooking\nSwim in spring-fed pool!\nTTFC Option: First Class #6e - water line rescue\nAstronomy MB wrap-up\nFree time for others\nSM Conferences and/or BORs\nAll adults must take Safe Swim Defense:\nhttps://www.capitolareascouting.org/training/adult/safe-swim-defense/\nDinner - Patrol Cooking\, James and Mike Bat grubmasters\n\nMonday:\nCold breakfast\nRoses and Thorns and Buds\nPack and depart for Lakeway\nArrive home approximately 3:00 pm\n\nNote: Campsites have a maximum of two vehicles and eight people except group site can have four vehicles and 16 people.\n\nNeeds:\nAssistant adult grubmaster\nAll adults attending must take Safe Swim Defense for safety.\nAdult to pull trailer?\nNot bringing smoker\n\nSIC:&nbsp;\nJames Ezell\njas_ezell@yahoo.com\n512-619-5750\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6446455
LOCATION:Location was not specified
END:VEVENT
