SUMMARY:NRA Shotgun Instructor Course
DESCRIPTION:NRA SHOTGUN INSTRUCTOR COURS\nNOTE: You must have previously taken the NRA Basic Instructor Training (BIT) course prior to taking this course.  BIT is offered with the NRA Rifle Instructor Course.\nAge Requirement: 21 and older to be a Certified Shotgun Instructor.&nbsp;\nCost: $80.00\nDescription: This course is for training and certification of NRA Shotgun Instructors. It includes the NRA Basics of Shotgun Shooting and the NRA Shotgun Instructor Training.   All participants must have experience at shooting shotguns.\nClass Size: This course is open to the first 20 who register.&nbsp;\nLocations:&nbsp;\nFriday - 8/22/2025 - 6:30 pm to 10:00 pm - Fickett Center -\nSaturday - 8/23/2025 -8:30 am to 10:00 pm - Fickett Center&nbsp;\nSaturday - 9/06/2025- 8:30 am to 6:00 pm   Shotgun Range and Hegn Lodge\, LPSR\nWhat to Bring: Pen or pencil. Dress casually.  Uniforms are not required. On Saturday 9/06/2025 -  Bring your own cleaning kit and lunch.  The council will supply all shotguns and ammunition.&nbsp;\nNRA Certification Fee: After completing the course\, there will be a fee to the NRA for certification.  The fee will be $30-$50 depending on whether or not you are a NRA member.\n&nbsp;For questions contact :Bill Agnell@gmail.com\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462113
LOCATION:Fickett Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462116@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250712T201828Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250905T171500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250906T180000
SUMMARY:Introduction to Outdoor Leader Training
DESCRIPTION:BSA Introduction to Outdoor Leadership Skill Pamphlet&nbsp;\nCapitol Area Council Chisholm Trail District invites you to participate in the Scoutmaster Leader-Specific Training \nIntroduction to Outdoor Leader Skills(IOLS) on September 5th and 6th\, 2025.\nWorking as patrols\, IOLS presents adult leaders with the practical knowledge needed to help Scouts to learn outdoor skills. The skills presented will closely follow the Scouts BSA Handbook and rank advancement requirements. Skills from Tenderfoot to First Class are covered in this training.\nAlong with Scoutmaster Specifics (online)\, this course is required of all direct contact leaders registered in Scouts BSA Troops to be considered \ntrained\n.  This is a required training course for all Scoutmaster/Assistant Scoutmasters and the Online Training must be completed prior to taking IOLS.\nIn addition\, anyone who may be attending campouts regularly should consider taking this class. The training is designed to help all adult leaders regardless of experience level feel comfortable performing and supervising these skills with youth.&nbsp;\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462116
LOCATION:Palm Valley Lutheran Church\, 2500 E Palm Valley Blvd\, Round Rock\, TX 78665
END:VEVENT
