BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462251@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250712T213348Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251114T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251115T200000
SUMMARY:Mega Training Fall 2025 - IOLS
DESCRIPTION:MEGA Training offers you the chance to take required training courses like Scoutmaster Leader-Specific Training\, Introduction to Outdoor Leader Skills (IOLS)\, or Basic Adult Leader Outdoor Orientation (BALOO). There are also optional courses\, including Chaplain Training\, Swimming and Water Rescue\, Paddle Craft Safety\, and more.\nScouts BSA Introduction to Outdoor Leadership Skills\nWorking as patrols\, this hands-on course provides adult leaders the practical outdoor skills they need to lead Scouts in the out-of-doors. Upon completion\, leaders should feel comfortable teaching Scouts the basic skills required to obtain the First Class rank. Along with Scoutmaster Specifics (online)\, this course is required of all direct contact leaders registered in Scouts BSA Troops to be considered \ntrained\n.&nbsp;\nClass Info\nFriday Check-in: 6pm at Lindsay Lodge. Please make sure you eat dinner on the way in to Lost Pines.\nSaturday: departure between 5pm and 8pm depending on length of discussions.\nAs a requirement for the class\, you must complete the Online Training prior to taking the class.\nPaperwork Needs\nBSA camping rules: All adults staying overnight must have a current Youth Protection Training certificate and must be registered with BSA in an adult fee-required position effective September 1\, 2023.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA Medical form parts A&amp;B.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA registration for every participant.&nbsp;\nFor all adults: bring a paper copy proof of unexpired YPT and your current BSA Leader Registration.\nSee https://www.scouting.org/health-and-safety/gss/gss01/ for more information.\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462251
LOCATION:Lindsay Lodget @ Lost Pines Scout Reservation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462258@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250712T213832Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251115T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251116T170000
SUMMARY:Mega Training Fall 2025 - Wilderness First Aid
DESCRIPTION:MEGA Training offers you the chance to take required training courses like Scoutmaster Leader-Specific Training\, Introduction to Outdoor Leader Skills (IOLS)\, or Basic Adult Leader Outdoor Orientation (BALOO). There are also optional courses\, including Chaplain Training\, Swimming and Water Rescue\, Paddle Craft Safety\, and more.\nBSA Wilderness First Aid and CPR/AED\nThis is an Emergency Care and Safety Institute (ECSI) online hybrid course.\nAfter registration\, you will be emailed access codes for Wilderness First Aid and CPR/AED along with instructions to access the course.  If you need help with your access codes\, please email wfa@troop550.org.\nWilderness First Aid:\nStudents are enrolled in a hybrid class - 8 hours of course content is accessed online\, to be completed at your convenience.  The online class must be completed before the scheduled skills evalutation at MEGA Training.  The skills evaluation is approximately 8 hours of skills practice and evaluation.\nCPR/AED:\nStudents are enrolled in an online class\, approximately 2 hours of online content. The online class must be completed before the scheduled skills evalutation at MEGA Training.  We offer Adult\, Child and Infant CPR instruction.  We use Prestan CPR dummies with feedback for compression effectiveness and rate.\nSkills Evaluation:\nWilderness First Aid and CPR/AED skills evaluations are scheduled on the same day.  This is the in person day you signed up for at MEGA. The skills evaluation covers everything from removing gloves\, assessments/paperwork\, inhaler use\, epipens\, bleeding control\, tourniquets (commercial and improvised)\, CPR\, AED\, choking\, bone/joint injuries and lots and lots of splinting.  It's all open book - just like it would be in the field - and we'll have skills reference binders to assist you.  Instructors will cover each skill and practice until everyone is comfortable with it.&nbsp;\nCertification:\nUpon completion of Wilderness First Aid and CPR/AED\, students are issued an ECSI Certificate of Completion.  Renewal is recommended after 2 years.  This Certificate of Completion meets the requirement for Scouting America High Adventure Base Wilderness First Aid and CPR/AED training.\nEligibility:\nAdults and youth are eligible to take CPR/AED classes.\nAdults and youth age 14+ are eligible to take Wilderness First Aid.\nMinimum required for the course: 6.  Maximum: 20.&nbsp;\nThe skills evaluation will be completed in one day - camping is not required.\nPaperwork Needs\nBSA camping rules: All adults staying overnight must have a current Youth Protection Training certificate and must be registered with BSA in an adult fee-required position effective September 1\, 2023.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA Medical form parts A&amp;B.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA registration for every participant.&nbsp;\nFor all adults: bring a paper copy proof of unexpired YPT and your current BSA Leader Registration.\nSee https://www.scouting.org/health-and-safety/gss/gss01/ for more information.\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462258
LOCATION:Lost Pines Scout Reservation
END:VEVENT
