SUMMARY:SCOUT SUNDAY
DESCRIPTION:SCOUT SUNDAYWE WILL NEED VOLUNTEERS DRESSED IN CLASS A UNIFORMS TO HELP AS DESCRIBED BELOW IN SHIFTS FROM 9 AM TO 12:15.PLEASE USE THE RSVP FUNCTION TO INDICATE YOUR INTEREST TO PARTICIPATE. THANKSWe'd love to welcomeÂ yall on Sunday 2/8 to hold open the exterior doors of the church and welcome our guests. This will be a great way to showÂ your presence as a followup to Baptism Sunday\, help out and get some direct interaction with us! The usual Sunday morning volunteer team is aware and will be ready to welcome the scouts.Â Scouts and their families are welcome to attend the church services between the below times\, if desired!Â Times:Â 9a-9:35ish: VOLUNTEERS NEEDED*Service is from 9:30a-10:30a10:20a-11:15a: VOLUNTEERS NEEDED*Service is from 11a-12p11:50a-12:15p: VOLUNTEERS NEEDEDDoor Greeting Locations:Â -Family entrance from the lower parking lot-Clubhouse entrance from lower Main Street-Elevator entrance from lower Main Street-Worship Center main entrance from the upper parking lot*Well aim for no more than 2 scouts per door\, and if there are more older scouts can be stationed in the parking lot to direct cars to open spots (pending scout and parent comfortability and safety needs).Â I will be on campus mostly around the Atrium any time before 9:30 to greet and answer any questions. Scouts can also arrive at any time\, but theres really no prep other than arriving at the doors. =\nKristin BrennerExecutive Director of Worship and Communications | Lakeway Churchoffice phone: 512-261-6331 x225at my desk: Monday-Thursdayin the Church Atrium: Sunday
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462416
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
