SUMMARY:Order of the Arrow Spring Assembly
DESCRIPTION:Tonkawa Lodge Assemblies are opportunities for those elected to become members of the Order of the Arrow. Assemblies normally take place at Lost Pines Scout Reservation in Bastrop. Commonly known as The Ordeal\, candidates will meet a series of challenges that will foster self-reflection and test their commitment to a life of cheerful service. For existing members\, Assembly Weekend offers a chance to build friendships and serve Scouting in meaningful ways.\nNew candidates\, you will receive a Candidate Information Packet in your email. Please read through the Candidate Information Packet as it contains important details for the weekend. Your dues for 2026 are included with your registration fee.\nExisting members must have paid their annual dues to attend Assembly. You may pay your dues upon arrival if they havent already been paid.\nEveryone must bring a non-returnable hard copy of your BSA health form (parts A &amp; B only).&nbsp;\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462526
LOCATION:Lost Pines Scout Reservation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462527@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T002501Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260525T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260525T120000
SUMMARY:Lakeway Assisted Living - Flag Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Lakeway Assisted Living - Flag Ceremony\nI'm looking for Troop 52 Volunteer Scouts to help with the flag ceremony. Please mark RSVP to let me know who can help.\nThe actual event will start at 10:30 a.m. It would be great if everyone could arrive at 10 a.m. to quickly review the plan together.&nbsp;\nAt 10:30\, we will have everyone head out to the parking lot by the flag pole\, where the troops can lower the old flag and raise the new one . We will also have taps playing during this time.&nbsp;\nAfter this\, we plan to have the residents go inside to package the donated items to send off to troops. You are all welcome to stay and assist with this. We would love for the troops to stay with the residents for lunch if you can. If not\, no worries! Let me know what works best for you all!&nbsp;\nYIS\nTray Bates\nScoutmaster\, Troop 52\nKey Contact for Lake Travis Independent Living:\nHaley Vick\, Sales Director\nLake Travis Independent Living\, A SPECTRUM RETIREMENT COMMUNITY&nbsp;\n302 Medical Pkwy.&nbsp;\nLakeway\, TX 78738&nbsp;\nph: 512.501.3488&nbsp;\nhaley.vick@spectrumretirement.com&nbsp;\nwww.LakeTravisIndependentLiving.com\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462527
LOCATION:Arbor Terrace Lakeway Assisted Living Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462531@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T003513Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260508T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260510T200000
SUMMARY:Mega Training Spring 2026 - IOLS
DESCRIPTION:MEGA Training offers you the chance to take required training courses like Scoutmaster Leader-Specific Training\, Introduction to Outdoor Leader Skills (IOLS)\, or Basic Adult Leader Outdoor Orientation (BALOO). There are also optional courses\, including Chaplain Training\, Swimming and Water Rescue\, Paddle Craft Safety\, and more.\nScouts BSA Introduction to Outdoor Leadership Skills\nWorking as patrols\, this hands-on course provides adult leaders the practical outdoor skills they need to lead Scouts in the out-of-doors. Upon completion\, leaders should feel comfortable teaching Scouts the basic skills required to obtain the First Class rank. Along with Scoutmaster Specifics (online)\, this course is required of all direct contact leaders registered in Scouts BSA Troops to be considered \ntrained\n.&nbsp;\nClass Info\nFriday Check-in: 6pm at Lindsay Lodge. Please make sure you eat dinner on the way in to Lost Pines.\nSaturday: departure between 5pm and 8pm depending on length of discussions.\nAs a requirement for the class\, you must complete the Online Training prior to taking the class.\n&nbsp;Paperwork Needs\nBSA camping rules: All adults staying overnight must have a current Youth Protection Training certificate and must be registered with BSA in an adult fee-required position effective September 1\, 2023.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA Medical form parts A&amp;B.\nFor every participant: bring a paper copy of your BSA registration for every participant.&nbsp;\nFor all adults: bring a paper copy proof of unexpired YPT and your current BSA Leader Registration.\nSee https://www.scouting.org/health-and-safety/gss/gss01/ for more information.\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462531
LOCATION:Lost Pines Scout Reservation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
