BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462569@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T005846Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260731T234500
SUMMARY:2026 National Jamboree
DESCRIPTION:The BSA National Jamboree is a gathering\, or jamboree\, of thousands of members of the Boy Scouts of America\, usually held every four years and organized by the National Council of the Boy Scouts of America.  Referred to as \nthe Jamboree\n\, \nJambo\n\, or NSJ\, Scouts from all over the nation and world have the opportunity to attend.\nThey are considered to be one of several unique experiences that the Boy Scouts of America offers.  The first jamboree was scheduled to be held in 1935 in Washington\, D.C. to celebrate the 25th anniversary of Scouting\, but was delayed two years after being cancelled due to a polio outbreak.  The 1937 jamboree in Washington attracted 25\,000 Scouts\, who camped around the Washington Monument and Tidal Basin.\nMinimum of 12 years of age on or before the first day of the Jamboree.\nDate:  July 22-31\, 2026\nFees:  $3\,000/participant (youth or adult)\nFees include:\nJamboree Admission\nRoundtrip Air Transportation to Charlotte\, NC.\nBus transportation to/from the Summit Bechtel Reserve\nShirts\, patches\, neckerchiefs\, etc.\nPreparation shakedowns\nMore...\nA payment schedule has been set up to pay participant fees - six $500 payments.\nAt registration - $500.00 before 04-30-2025\nFirst Payment - $500.00 due 06-30-2025\nSecond Payment - $500.00 due 08-31-2025\nThird Payment - $500.00 due 10-31-2025\nFourth Payment - $500.00 due 01-31-2026\nFifth Payment - $500.00 due 03-31-2026\nGo to the following Jamboree sites for more information:\nNational Scouting America site - https://jamboree.scouting.org\nCapitol Area Council site - https://www.bsacac.org/activities/jamborees/\nDeadline to register is October 31\, 2025!\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462569
LOCATION:Summit Bechtel Reserve
END:VEVENT
