DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260727T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260727T203000
SUMMARY:Patrol Leaders Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC) Planning MeetingThe Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC) is where the youth leaders of Troop 52 plan and lead the troop's program. This meeting is attended by the Senior Patrol Leader\, Assistant Senior Patrol Leaders\, Patrol Leaders\, Troop Guides\, andÂ all Scouts serving in a Position of Responsibility (POR)\, including positions such as Quartermaster\, Scribe\, Historian\, Librarian\, Chaplain Aide\, Instructor\, Order of the Arrow Representative\, Webmaster\, Den Chief\, Leave No Trace Trainer\, Bugler\, and any other currently serving youth leaders.During the meeting\, these Scouts work together to evaluate recent troop meetings and campouts\, discuss upcoming activities\, and develop the plans for future troop meetings\, campouts\, service projects\, and special events. Each youth leader provides input from their area of responsibility\, helping ensure that every aspect of the troop program is coordinated and prepared in advance.The PLC is responsible for ensuring that troop meetings are engaging\, well-organized\, and support the advancement\, leadership development\, and outdoor program goals of the troop. Adult leaders serve as mentors and advisors\, while the Scouts take the lead in planning\, decision-making\, and executing the troop's annual program.Meeting Objectives:Review recent troop meetings\, campouts\, and special events.Plan agendas and activities for upcoming troop meetings.Assign leadership responsibilities for future meetings and events.Coordinate upcoming campouts\, service projects\, Courts of Honor\, and other troop activities.Identify advancement opportunities to incorporate into the troop program.Review equipment\, transportation\, communications\, and other logistical needs.Discuss patrol concerns\, troop needs\, and ideas for improving the Scouting experience.Strengthen youth leadership\, communication\, planning\, and teamwork.The Patrol Leaders' Council is one of the most important leadership meetings in the troop. It is where Scouts with leadership responsibilities collaborate\, solve problems\, and make decisions that shape the troop's program. By planning ahead and working together\, the PLC ensures that Troop 52 continues to provide a fun\, organized\, and truly Scout-led experience for every member.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462575
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462576@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260803T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260803T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Scout Trailer Clean-Out &amp; Gear Inventory NightHelp us get Troop 52 ready for a great year of camping! During this meeting\, the entire troop will work together to unload all equipment from the Scout trailer\, organize and inspect our gear\, and ensure everything is in good working order.Each patrol will inventory the contents of its Patrol Box\, identify missing\, damaged\, or worn-out items\, and create a list of supplies that need to be replaced before our next campout. Scouts will also inspect troop equipment\, clean and organize gear\, and help repack the trailer using our standard layout so everything is easy to find and ready to go.Meeting Objectives:Unload all equipment from the Scout trailer.Clean and inspect troop gear.Inventory each Patrol Box.Document missing or damaged equipment.Prepare a purchase list for replacement items.Repack the trailer in an organized\, standardized manner.Ensure the trailer is fully stocked and camp-ready for our next outing.This meeting is an important part of maintaining our troop equipment and teaches Scouts responsibility\, organization\, teamwork\, and stewardship of shared resources. Every Scout's participation is needed to make sure Troop 52 is prepared for a successful camping season.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462576
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462577@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260810T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260810T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Red Trailer Storage Organization &amp; Inventory NightThe Troop 52 Red Trailer serves as our primary storage unit for troop equipment\, supplies\, and program materials. During this meeting\, Scouts will work together to completely unload the trailer\, clean the interior\, and organize all stored items to ensure everything is accessible\, accounted for\, and ready for future use.As equipment is removed\, Scouts will inspect each item to determine whether it should be kept\, repaired\, replaced\, or discarded. Usable equipment will be neatly reorganized and returned to the trailer in a logical\, efficient layout. Items that are no longer serviceable or have reached the end of their useful life will be separated and staged in the rear of the trailer for proper disposal or replacement at a later date.Meeting Objectives:Completely unload the Red Trailer.Clean the trailer interior and storage areas.Inspect and organize all stored troop equipment and supplies.Identify items that should be retained\, repaired\, replaced\, or discarded.Stage unwanted or damaged items in the rear of the trailer for future disposal.Return all usable equipment to the trailer in a clean\, organized\, and standardized arrangement.Prepare the trailer for efficient storage and easy access throughout the year.This meeting helps ensure Troop 52's long-term equipment and storage remain organized and functional while teaching Scouts responsibility\, teamwork\, organization\, and stewardship of troop property. Every Scout's participation is important in helping maintain one of the troop's most valuable resources.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462577
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462578@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260817T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260817T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Patrol Spirit &amp; Court of Honor Preparation NightThis meeting is dedicated to building patrol pride while preparing for our upcoming Court of Honor. Each patrol will assemble its patrol flag onto its flagpole and add decorations and finishing touches that showcase the patrol's identity\, creativity\, and Scout spirit. Patrols are encouraged to work together to create a flag and pole they will be proud to carry and display during troop events.While patrols are working on their flags\, troop leaders will conduct Scoutmaster Conferences and Boards of Review for eligible Scouts. These advancement conferences are an important opportunity for Scouts to complete rank requirements and ensure all advancement records are current before the upcoming Court of Honor.Meeting Objectives:Assemble each patrol flag onto its flagpole.Decorate and personalize patrol flags and flagpoles.Promote patrol identity\, teamwork\, and Scout spirit.Complete Scoutmaster Conferences for eligible Scouts.Conduct Boards of Review for eligible Scouts.Verify and update advancement records in preparation for the Court of Honor.Ensure all eligible rank advancements and awards are ready for recognition.This meeting combines creativity\, teamwork\, and advancement\, helping each Scout and patrol prepare for one of the troop's most important recognition events of the year. Every Scout is encouraged to participate and help make their patrol stand out at the upcoming Court of Honor.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462578
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462579@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260824T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260824T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Advancement &amp; Court of Honor Readiness NightThis is our final troop meeting before the upcoming Court of Honor\, making it an important opportunity to ensure every eligible Scout is prepared for recognition. The primary focus of the evening will be completing Scoutmaster Conferences and Boards of Review so that advancement records are finalized and all eligible ranks and awards can be included in the Court of Honor.Scouts who are not participating in conferences or boards will use this time to complete any remaining Patrol Spirit projects\, including final assembly\, decorating\, or finishing touches on their patrol flags and flagpoles. By the end of the meeting\, both our advancement records and patrol displays should be complete and ready for the ceremony.Meeting Objectives:Complete Scoutmaster Conferences for all eligible Scouts.Conduct Boards of Review for all eligible Scouts.Verify and finalize advancement records for the Court of Honor.Complete any remaining Patrol Spirit projects.Finish assembling and decorating patrol flags and flagpoles.Ensure the troop is fully prepared for a successful and meaningful Court of Honor.This meeting is the final step in preparing for one of the troop's most important recognition events. Every Scout is encouraged to participate so that we can celebrate accomplishments\, recognize advancement\, and showcase the pride and spirit of each patrol at the Court of Honor.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462579
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462580@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260831T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260831T203000
SUMMARY:Court of Honor
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Court of HonorJoin us as we celebrate the accomplishments and advancement of our Scouts at the Troop 52 Court of Honor\, held in the Chapel. This special ceremony recognizes Scouts who have earned new ranks\, merit badges\, and other awards since our last Court of Honor. Families are encouraged to attend as we honor the hard work\, dedication\, and achievements of our Scouts.Uniform &amp; Appearance\nThis is a formal troop event. All Scouts should wear a completeÂ Class A (Field) Uniform\, including:Official Scout shirtOfficial Scout pants or shortsScout belt and socks (if available) with close-toed shoes\, no crocks.Neckerchief and slideMerit Badge SashÂ (for Scouts who have earned merit badges)Please arrive in a neat\, complete uniform to help make this a memorable and respectful ceremony.Volunteers Needed\nWe are looking for Scouts to serve in a variety of speaking and leadership roles during the ceremony\, including the opening\, introductions\, award presentations\, readings\, and closing. Participating in these roles is an excellent opportunity to fulfillÂ public speaking requirements for the Communications Merit BadgeÂ while helping make the Court of Honor a success. Please let the Scoutmaster know if you are interested in volunteering.We look forward to celebrating the achievements of every Scout and sharing this special evening with our troop families.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462580
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462582@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Colorado Bend Campout Preparation NightGet ready for our upcoming campout atÂ Colorado Bend State Park! This meeting is designed to help Scouts prepare for a successful weekend outdoors by reviewing the gear they will need\, how Troop 52 camping equipment is organized\, and the best practices for packing and transporting gear to their campsite.Scouts will receive an overview of the troop's camping equipment\, including patrol gear\, cooking equipment\, tents\, and shared supplies. We will also discuss what personal gear each Scout should bring\, how to pack efficiently\, and how to transport equipment from the trailer to the campsite while following Leave No Trace principles and working together as a patrol.Meeting Objectives:Learn about Troop 52's camping equipment and how it is organized.Review patrol gear and each Scout's responsibilities.Discuss the personal gear needed for the Colorado Bend campout.Learn effective packing techniques for comfort and efficiency.Understand how to transport troop and personal gear from the trailer to the campsite.Review campsite setup\, organization\, and Leave No Trace expectations.Ensure every Scout is prepared for a safe\, enjoyable\, and successful campout.Whether you're attending your first campout or your fiftieth\, this meeting will help everyone arrive prepared and ready to enjoy everything Colorado Bend State Park has to offer.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462582
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6462583@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250713T010224Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260921T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260921T203000
SUMMARY:Troop Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Campout Final Preparation NightThis is our final troop meeting before departing for our campout atÂ Colorado Bend State Park. The focus of the evening will be making sure each patrol is fully prepared by completing meal planning\, organizing duty assignments\, and developing campfire skits to build patrol spirit and provide entertainment during the campout.Each patrol will work together to create a menu for the weekend\, develop shopping lists\, assign cooking and cleanup responsibilities\, and confirm that all food and equipment needs have been addressed. Patrols will also brainstorm\, practice\, and refine their campfire skits so they are ready to perform during the evening campfire program.Meeting Objectives:Complete patrol meal planning for the campout.Create grocery shopping lists and identify grubmaster (food purchasers).Assign patrol cooking\, cleanup\, and campsite responsibilities.Review final equipment and packing needs.Develop and rehearse patrol campfire skits.Build patrol teamwork\, communication\, and Scout spirit.Ensure every patrol is fully prepared for a successful campout.By the end of the meeting\, each patrol should have its meals planned\, duties assigned\, skits rehearsed\, and all preparations complete so everyone can arrive at Colorado Bend State Park ready for a fun\, safe\, and memorable camping adventure.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6462583
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - Fellowship Hall
END:VEVENT
