BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6470632@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250717T231821Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251108T140000
SUMMARY:Scouturday Speedfest
DESCRIPTION:Scouturday Speedfest @ Circuit of the Americas is the celebration of our "Race into Scouting" membership campaign. This special event is open to ANYONE in Scouting. From Pinewood Derby to pro-level race cars\, there's fun for the whole family! Event Activities include: Pinewood Derby at the Paddock\, Formula One Car Display\, Formula Four Car Display\, COTA Karting\, Racing Simulators\, Texas State University Bobcat Racing Team\, Public Service Vehicle Displays\, and more!  www.capitolareascouting.org/speedfest\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6470632
LOCATION:Circuit of the Americas\, 9201 Circuit of the Americas Blvd.\, Del Valle TX 78617
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6485659@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250727T141932Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250823T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250823T110000
SUMMARY:TTFC: Navigation & Orienteering; First Class 4a-b
DESCRIPTION:Come test your orienteering skills as you navigate a six-waypoint course.  Work as a team to find all the clues to the key phrase and earn a prize.\nFor those that need it\, we will cover First Class requirements 4a\, b.\nStar Scouts also have an opportunity to earn Life Scout requirement 6 by assisting with the setup of the course and teaching orienteering skills to other Scouts using the Teaching EDGE method.\n\n\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6485659
LOCATION:Lakeway City Park - Lower Level
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6489399@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250728T212826Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250913T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250913T110000
SUMMARY:Trial to First Class: Tenderfoot 5a-c, 6c
DESCRIPTION:We will be focusing this session on Tenderfoot requirements 5a-c - Hiking Safety\, 6c Personal Fitness Part 2\nFitness (part 2): building from Fitness part 1 (Tenderfoot 6a\,b) testing your improvement over 30 days from the baseline\nImportant: Wear athletic shoes and bring a water bottle\nNOTE: we can also baseline anyone for 6a\,b if you missed part 1\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6489399
LOCATION:Lakeway City Park - Lower Level
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6489554@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250728T213918Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251004T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251004T113000
SUMMARY:Trail to First Class: Firem'n Chit, 2nd Class 2a-d
DESCRIPTION:Earning the Firem n Chit award is one of the first steps a Scout takes toward mastering fire safety. Scouts are known for camping and treating the wilderness with respect\, but that can t be done without using fire safely and responsibly. The Firem n Chit will teach you the key principles for safe fire usage! This certification grants a Scout the right to carry matches and build campfires. In this training session\, you will demonstrate that you understand your responsibility to do the eight requirements.\nWe will also cover Second Class 2a-d for building fires for campout cooking.\nImportant: please wear closed toed shoes\nNOTE: please do not bring your own fire starting tools or materials; we will supply all tools and materials\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6489554
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6490108@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250729T003258Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251027T190000
SUMMARY:Trail to First Class: Knot Fest!
DESCRIPTION:&nbsp;We will have three different knot-tying stations:\nTenderfoot 3a-c\, 8\nSecond Class 2f-g&nbsp;\nFirst Class 3a-d\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6490108
LOCATION:Lakeway Church 
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6490120@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250729T004200Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251109T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251109T120000
SUMMARY:Trail to First Class: SC 3a-d, 4; FC 5a-d
DESCRIPTION:This session will revolve around a 5-mile hike around Hamilton Greenbelt.\nWe will cover Second Class Requirements 3a-d\, 4 and some of First Class 5a-d\nFor those just needing 2nd class 4 or 1st class 5a-d\, we will separate into groups to complete requirements separately.\nFor those doing the hike\, please bring a small backpack with water\, a compass (if you have one)\, hat\, good walking shoes and some snacks.\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6490120
LOCATION:Hamilton Greenbelt 1173 Lohmans Crossing Rd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6535979@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250813T011418Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250928T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250928T140000
SUMMARY:Troop 52 Cookout @ Lakeway Church
DESCRIPTION:Cooking Burgers and Hotdogs for Church after Baptism. Need Adults to help cook and Scouts to help serve. Dressing in Class A Uniforms\nPLEASE RSVP!\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6535979
LOCATION:Location was not specified
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6598963@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250831T144959Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251014T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251014T200000
SUMMARY:Fly Fishing MB Workshop: Requirements 3 & 4
DESCRIPTION:For those working on the Fly Fishing MB\, we will be working on requirements 3 and 4.\nSportsmans Finest has offered their expertise and gear to the Troop during their weekly fly-tying sessions.&nbsp;&nbsp;\nThis is one of two sessions on September 30 and October 7.  You can attend one or both of these sessions and we will work on both requirements during both sessions.\n3. Demonstrate how to tie proper knots to prepare a fly rod for fishing:\n"	(a) Tie backing to the arbor of a fly reel spool using an arbor knot.\n"	(b) Tie backing to the fly line using a nail (tube) knot.\n"	(c) Attach a leader to the fly line using a nail (tube) knot or a loop-to-loop connection.\n"	(d) Add a tippet to a leader using a surgeon's knot or a loop-to-loop connection.\n"	(e) Tie a fly onto the terminal end of the leader using an improved clinch knot.\n4. Explain how and when each of the following types of flies is used: dry flies\, wet flies\, nymphs\, streamers\, bass bugs\, poppers\, and saltwater flies. Tell what each one imitates. Tie at least two types of the flies mentioned in this requirement.\n\n\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6598963
LOCATION:Sportsman's Finest
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6598966@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20250831T145255Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251007T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251007T200000
SUMMARY:Fly Fishing MB Workshop: Requirements 3 & 4
DESCRIPTION:For those working on the Fly Fishing MB\, we will be working on requirements 3 and 4.\nSportsmans Finest has offered their expertise and gear to the Troop during their weekly fly-tying sessions.&nbsp;&nbsp;\nThis is one of two sessions on September 30 and October 7.  You can attend one or both of these sessions and we will work on both requirements during both sessions.\n3. Demonstrate how to tie proper knots to prepare a fly rod for fishing:\n"	(a) Tie backing to the arbor of a fly reel spool using an arbor knot.\n"	(b) Tie backing to the fly line using a nail (tube) knot.\n"	(c) Attach a leader to the fly line using a nail (tube) knot or a loop-to-loop connection.\n"	(d) Add a tippet to a leader using a surgeon's knot or a loop-to-loop connection.\n"	(e) Tie a fly onto the terminal end of the leader using an improved clinch knot.\n4. Explain how and when each of the following types of flies is used: dry flies\, wet flies\, nymphs\, streamers\, bass bugs\, poppers\, and saltwater flies. Tell what each one imitates. Tie at least two types of the flies mentioned in this requirement.\n\n\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6598966
LOCATION:Sportsman's Finest
END:VEVENT
