BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6750832@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20251119T014344Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251201T190000
SUMMARY:TTFC:  Second Class 6a-e
DESCRIPTION:We will be covering Second Class Requirement 6: First Aid and Emergency Preparedness\nI am looking for a FULLY PREPARED Star Scout who wants to get signed off on Life requirement 6\na.	Demonstrate first aid for the following:\no	Object in the eye\no	Bite of a warm-blooded animal\no	Puncture wounds from a splinter\, nail\, and fishhook\no	Serious burns (partial thickness\, or second-degree)\no	Heat exhaustion\no	Shock\no	Heatstroke\, dehydration\, hypothermia\, and hyperventilation\nb.	Show what to do for \nhurrycases of stopped breathing\, stroke\, severe bleeding\, and ingested poisoning.\nc.	Tell what you can do while on a campout or hike to prevent or reduce the occurrence of the injuries listed in Second Class requirements 6a and 6b.\nd.	Explain what to do in case of accidents that require emergency response in the home and backcountry. Explain what constitutes an emergency and what information you will need to provide to a responder.\ne.	Tell how you should respond if you come upon the scene of a vehicular accident.\n\n\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6750832
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6757048@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20251124T144012Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251206T140000
SUMMARY:Srijay Jagarlamudi Eagle Project
DESCRIPTION:Project Leader: Srijay Jagarlamudi  Troop 52\nBeneficiary: Lakeway Parks &amp; Recreation\nDate: December 6th\, 2025\, 9:00 A.M.  2:00 P.M.\nLocation: 113 Trophy Drive\, The Hills\, TX 78738\nProject Goal: Enhance and formalize the existing entrance to establish a single\, clearly identifiable\, and accessible point of entry for all users.\nPROJECT SUMMARY\nWe will begin by cleaning up the flower beds\, removing dead plants and weeds. Next\, well plant native\, drought-tolerant species of four Texas sage bushes in the back (since they grow taller)\, and eight red yucca and eight lantana plants in the front. After planting\, well spread about 30 cubic yards of mulch along the trail. Finally\, well install split-rail fencing to make the path more visible\, digging 16-inch holes for each post. Each section of fencing will measure 10 feet\, for a total of 40 feet.\nWed love you to be part of this project. Any time you can offer will be sincerely appreciated\, and Scouts will earn community service hours for their participation.\nItems to bring: Work gloves\, Water bottle\, and a Great attitude!\nWe will provide Doughnuts in the morning and Pizza for lunch.\nSincerely\,\nSrijay Jagarlamudi\n
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6757048
LOCATION:Location was not specified
END:VEVENT
