DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260323T190000
SUMMARY:TTFC:  First Class 9a - Citizenship
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Phillip Davis\, who is currently serving as a Trustee on the Lake Travis ISD school board\, has volunteered his time to help scouts with this requirement.Â  See his bio below.Please RSVP for this one so we can be respectful of Mr. Davis time.I expect each of you to prepare questions with a focus on the Constitution's impact on Mr. Davis job and his obligations &amp; rights/duties as a citizen (e.g.\, voting\, jury\, taxes\, free speech).I also expect you to take notes and share those with your patrol and/or patrols Assistant Scoutmaster.Key Concepts to Discuss:Rights: Freedom of speech\, religion\, assembly\, property\, fair trial\, equal protection\, choosing leaders.Obligations/Responsibilities: Obeying laws\, paying taxes\, voting\, serving on juries\, helping the community.Dr. Davis was elected to the Board of Trustees in 2021. He is a graduate of Clemson University with a bachelors degree in Industrial Engineering and a Master of Business Administration degree with an emphasis in Operations Management. He received a Doctor of Philosophy degree in Management from the University of North Texas. He currently teaches and conducts research at Texas State University\, where he is an assistant professor and core course coordinator.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/6789506
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
