BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7028030@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260719T155343Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260804T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260804T203000
SUMMARY:Parent Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Troop Committee (Parent) MeetingThe Troop Committee Meeting is the monthly business meeting that supports the successful operation of Troop 52. While the troop's youth leaders plan and lead the Scouting program through the Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC)\, the Troop Committee provides the administrative\, financial\, and logistical support that enables the troop to deliver a safe\, well-organized\, and high-quality Scouting experience.All parents are encouraged to attend\, whether they currently serve on the committee or simply want to learn more about the troop's operations. This meeting is an excellent opportunity to stay informed\, ask questions\, volunteer\, and become involved in supporting our Scouts.Topics typically include upcoming campouts and activities\, transportation and logistics\, finances\, fundraising\, equipment needs\, advancement reporting\, membership\, training\, volunteer opportunities\, Eagle Scout projects\, long-range planning\, and any other business affecting the troop.Meeting Objectives:Ratify the Annual PlanReview upcoming troop meetings\, campouts\, and special events.Discuss troop finances\, fundraising\, and budget needs.Coordinate transportation\, equipment\, and logistical support.Review advancement reporting and upcoming Courts of Honor.Discuss Eagle Scout projects and other service opportunities.Recruit volunteers for upcoming troop activities.Review safety\, training\, and policy updates.Address troop business and answer parent questions.Ensure the troop has the resources and support needed for a successful Scout-led program.The Troop Committee plays a vital role in the success of Troop 52. By supporting the Scouts and their youth leaders behind the scenes\, committee members and parents help create opportunities for leadership\, adventure\, personal growth\, and lifelong memories for every Scout.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7028030
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7034341@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260723T003945Z
ORGANIZER:Nicolas Sfeir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260731T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260731T133000
SUMMARY:Swimming MB and Swim Test
DESCRIPTION:Howdy Troop 52 Scouts\,I hope everyone is having a good summer break.We will be holding the Swimming MB and a Swim Test at Nitro on July 31st at noon.Nitro gave us a discounted rate of $30 per scout for the Swimming MB\, and if you're only doing the Swim Test\, we recommend a gratuity to the lifeguard on duty who will be supervising the scouts.You can Venmo me @Nicolas-SfeirThe intent of this event is for the scouts to show up ready to demonstrate the requirements. Nitro will not teach the different strokes.We will tackle the following MB requirements. I have included the link below for reference:2 (if you don't have aÂ 2026 "Swimmer"Â classification on the Scouting America swimmer test)3 a\, b\, c\, d\, e45 a\, b6 a\, b\, c7 a\, b\, c8https://www.scouting.org/merit-badges/swimming/I will need help from ourÂ SwimmingÂ MeritÂ BadgeÂ Counselors with the remaining requirements (1\, 6b\, 9) and MB sign-offs.\nPlease complete the waiver prior to the event. Link below.\nhttps://waiver.smartwaiver.com/e/C5czfR7ruCPytQtx4MqCk/Feel free to reach out to me with any questions or concerns.YIS\,Nico Sfeir702-604-1178
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7034341
LOCATION:Nitro Swim Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7038137@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260725T212321Z
ORGANIZER:Trevor Montgomery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260925T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260927T234500
SUMMARY:Fun Campout
DESCRIPTION:This will be a "FUN" campout! We will be camping right along the banks of the Colorado River in Colorado Bend State Park. Saturday morning we will be doing the Wild Cave Tour hosted by the Nichols Outdoor Adventures company (optional and for an additional fee). In the afternoon\, we will be hiking the Gorman Falls trail to see the wonders of the falls - a hidden gem\, after which we will cool off in the waters of the Colorado river.  This will be a patrol cooking campout and we will prepare meal plans for the campout at the Troop meeting on Monday 9/21.NOTE: Any Scout wishing to swim or even wade in the river must have a CURRENT swim classification.IMPORTANT: Â Registration requires two steps:RSVP on Scoutbook (here); RSVP deadline for Fun campout is 5PM 9/22/2026; . Â If you have not RSVP-ed by this date/time you will not be considered a participant and cannot attend.Pay for the campout (this item in the store); Cost for Scouts $30 and Adults is $35. If you do not cancel registration before 5pm on Tuesday before the Campout/Event. The payments made will only be counted towards the specific Campout/Event and not carried over as credit for future payments. If you have not paid for a previous campout\, then you must pay this past due campout fee before your registration will be accepted. If you have any questions then please contact the SIC.Friday6PM:  Depart Lake Travis Middle School. It is just under a 2-hour drive so Scouts must be prepared to arrive and setup camp in the dark. That means headlamp\, tent\, sleeping gear easily accessible9PM:  Cracker barrel10PM:  Lights outSaturday7-9AM: Breakfast and cleanup9AM-12PM: Cave adventure tour - optional and for an additional fee12PM-1:30PM: Lunch2-4PM: Gorman Falls hike4PM-6PM: Free time; swim/wade/fish in the river - bring swimsuit and / or fishing gear6PM-8PM: Dinner8-9PM: Campfire program10PM:  Lights outSunday7-9AM: Breakfast and cleanup9-11AM: Breakdown camp\, patrol lines\, roses and thorns11AM: Depart CBSP2PM: Arrive at LTMS SIC: Â Trevor Montgomery Â 512.663.4388Trailer-puller: Â TBDBat Patrol Grubmaster: Â Trevor Montgomery &amp; Dave Kraft
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7038137
LOCATION:Colorado Bend State Park
END:VEVENT
