BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7040257@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260726T210928Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20270308T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20270308T210000
SUMMARY:Crossover Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Webelos Crossover CeremonyFollowing our annual Pioneering Campout\, Troop 52 will proudly host itsÂ Webelos Crossover CeremonyÂ at theÂ Barton Creek Habitat Preserve Pavilion. During the campout\, our Scouts will construct the ceremonial crossover bridge using pioneering skills\, creating a meaningful symbol of each Webelos Scout's transition into Scouts BSA.This special ceremony is one of the most memorable traditions in Scouting. Troop 52 Scouts will lead the ceremony by welcoming Webelos Scouts and their families\, sharing the significance of the Scout Oath and Scout Law\, and recognizing each Scout as they take the next step in their Scouting journey. As each Webelos Scout crosses the bridge\, they officially begin their adventure as a member of Troop 52.Following the ceremony\, Troop 52 Scouts will assist with packing and storing troop equipment while families\, our newest Scouts\, and their parents are invited to gather for fellowship and enjoy Dutch oven cobbler prepared by the troop's adult leaders.Ceremony Highlights:Welcome Webelos Scouts and their families.Troop 52 Scouts lead the Crossover Ceremony.Webelos Scouts cross the pioneering bridge into Troop 52.Celebrate the beginning of each Scout's Scouts BSA journey.Fellowship with new Scouts\, families\, and troop members.Enjoy Dutch oven cobbler prepared by the troop's adult leaders.Troop members assist with cleanup and equipment storage following the event.The Webelos Crossover Ceremony marks the beginning of an exciting new chapter in Scouting. We look forward to welcoming our newest Scouts into Troop 52 and celebrating this important milestone with their families and our troop community.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7040257
LOCATION:Barton Creek Habitat Preserve Pavillion (Nature Conservancy entrance next to Lake Hills Church off of Bee Cave Road)
END:VEVENT
