ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20270412T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20270412T203000
SUMMARY:Patrol Leader Council
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC) Planning MeetingThe Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC) is where the youth leaders of Troop 52 plan and lead the troop's program. This meeting is attended by the Senior Patrol Leader\, Assistant Senior Patrol Leaders\, Patrol Leaders\, Troop Guides\, andÂ all Scouts serving in a Position of Responsibility (POR)\, including positions such as Quartermaster\, Scribe\, Historian\, Librarian\, Chaplain Aide\, Instructor\, Order of the Arrow Representative\, Webmaster\, Den Chief\, Leave No Trace Trainer\, Bugler\, and any other currently serving youth leaders.During the meeting\, these Scouts work together to evaluate recent troop meetings and campouts\, discuss upcoming activities\, and develop the plans for future troop meetings\, campouts\, service projects\, and special events. Each youth leader provides input from their area of responsibility\, helping ensure that every aspect of the troop program is coordinated and prepared in advance.The PLC is responsible for ensuring that troop meetings are engaging\, well-organized\, and support the advancement\, leadership development\, and outdoor program goals of the troop. Adult leaders serve as mentors and advisors\, while the Scouts take the lead in planning\, decision-making\, and executing the troop's annual program.Meeting Objectives:Review recent troop meetings\, campouts\, and special events.Plan agendas and activities for upcoming troop meetings.Assign leadership responsibilities for future meetings and events.Coordinate upcoming campouts\, service projects\, Courts of Honor\, and other troop activities.Identify advancement opportunities to incorporate into the troop program.Review equipment\, transportation\, communications\, and other logistical needs.Discuss patrol concerns\, troop needs\, and ideas for improving the Scouting experience.Strengthen youth leadership\, communication\, planning\, and teamwork.The Patrol Leaders' Council is one of the most important leadership meetings in the troop. It is where Scouts with leadership responsibilities collaborate\, solve problems\, and make decisions that shape the troop's program. By planning ahead and working together\, the PLC ensures that Troop 52 continues to provide a fun\, organized\, and truly Scout-led experience for every member.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7040364
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7040369@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260726T212759Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20270413T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20270413T203000
SUMMARY:Parent Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Troop Committee (Parent) MeetingThe Troop Committee Meeting is the monthly business meeting that supports the successful operation of Troop 52. While the troop's youth leaders plan and lead the Scouting program through the Patrol Leaders' Council (PLC)\, the Troop Committee provides the administrative\, financial\, and logistical support that enables the troop to deliver a safe\, well-organized\, and high-quality Scouting experience.All parents are encouraged to attend\, whether they currently serve on the committee or simply want to learn more about the troop's operations. This meeting is an excellent opportunity to stay informed\, ask questions\, volunteer\, and become involved in supporting our Scouts.Topics typically include upcoming campouts and activities\, transportation and logistics\, finances\, fundraising\, equipment needs\, advancement reporting\, membership\, training\, volunteer opportunities\, Eagle Scout projects\, long-range planning\, and any other business affecting the troop.Meeting Objectives:Review upcoming troop meetings\, campouts\, and special events.Discuss troop finances\, fundraising\, and budget needs.Coordinate transportation\, equipment\, and logistical support.Review advancement reporting and upcoming Courts of Honor.Discuss Eagle Scout projects and other service opportunities.Recruit volunteers for upcoming troop activities.Review safety\, training\, and policy updates.Address troop business and answer parent questions.Ensure the troop has the resources and support needed for a successful Scout-led program.The Troop Committee plays a vital role in the success of Troop 52. By supporting the Scouts and their youth leaders behind the scenes\, committee members and parents help create opportunities for leadership\, adventure\, personal growth\, and lifelong memories for every Scout.
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7040369
LOCATION:Lakeway Church
END:VEVENT
