BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7052328@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260731T160946Z
ORGANIZER:Tracy Bates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260808T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260808T130000
SUMMARY:Landon Bates Eagle Scout Project
DESCRIPTION:Troop 52 Service Opportunity - Support Landon's Eagle Scout ProjectLandon Bates Eagle Project FlyerDate:Â Saturday\, August 8\, 2026\nTime:Â 8:30 a.m. - 1:00 p.m.\nLocation:Â Lakeway ChurchPlease come out and helpÂ Life Scout Landon BatesÂ complete his Eagle Scout Service Project benefiting theÂ Austin Wildlife Rescue Center. Volunteers will be building wooden wildlife shelter structures that will be delivered to the rescue center immediately following the project. This is a great opportunity to support a fellow Scout while earning service hours.Scouts who participate will earn Conservation Service Hours\, which count toward rank advancement and other Scouting service requirements. If you need conservation hours for advancement\, this is a great opportunity to get them while helping a fellow Scout achieve the rank of Eagle Scout.What to WearClosed-toe shoes (required)Work clothes that can get dirtySafety glasses or other eye protection (required)Work gloves (recommended)Hat and sunscreen (recommended)What to BringWater bottle (optional-we'll have plenty of drinks available)If you have one\, aÂ cordless drill/driverÂ with a charged battery would be helpful. We will have plenty of tools available\, so bringing one is optional.Food &amp; DrinksWe'll have everything you need to stay fueled and hydrated:Donuts and coffee during check-inPizza for lunchPlenty of cold water and GatoradeCoolers with ice throughout the projectComfort &amp; SafetyWe'll have Troop 52 pop-up tents set up to provide shade\, along with frequent water breaks to help everyone stay cool. A safety briefing will be held before work begins\, and experienced adults will supervise all tool use in accordance with BSA safety guidelines.Whether you can stay for the entire project or just part of the morning\, your help is greatly appreciated. The more volunteers we have\, the more efficiently we can complete the project while giving Landon the opportunity to demonstrate the leadership required for Eagle Scout.Thank you for supporting Landon and helping make a lasting impact for the Austin Wildlife Rescue Center. We look forward to seeing you on August 8!
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7052328
LOCATION:Lakeway Church - 2203 Lakeway Blvd\, Lakeway\, TX 78734
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7066275@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260805T155055Z
ORGANIZER:Nicolas Sfeir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260815T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260815T130000
SUMMARY:Maron Sfeir Eagle Project
DESCRIPTION:Howdy Scouts!I am organizing an Eagle Scout service project to benefit the LTYA Field of Dreams by replacing the backstop boards at three baseball fields\, supporting local athletics. The project\, which aims to improve safety by providing reliable backstops for players and spectators\, will enhance field quality for youth baseball and softball leagues while upgrading public facilities for future generations. The community is invited to join and support the project on August 15th from 8:00 AM to 12:00 PM at 13909 State Hwy 71\, Bee Cave\, TX 78730. Safety First: Please bring your closed-toe shoes\, hat\, work gloves\, sunscreen\, and a water bottle.Bring a hand drill if you have one.Donuts\, Gatorade\, and Pizzas will be provided. Please RSVP so I can get a headcount for the food.Thank you for supporting this project!Yours in Scouting\,Maron Sfeir
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7066275
LOCATION:Location was not specified
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7097526@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260815T224707Z
ORGANIZER:Nicolas Sfeir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260816T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260816T130000
SUMMARY:Maron Sfeir Eagle Project Part 2
DESCRIPTION:Howdy Scouts\,\nI wanted to thank everyone that attended today! It was a heck of an effort in this Central Texas heat.\nWe didn't quite finish today. We were overambitious with the scope and time of the project. We're going back at it tomorrow to finish it. The big lift was completed today. \nSame as always: bring sunscreen\, hat\, gloves\, closed-toe shoes\, and safety glasses. We will provide water\, Gatorade\, breakfast\, and lunch.\nThank you for your support!\nYIS\,Maron Sfeir
URL:https://advancements.scouting.org/calendar/event/7097526
LOCATION:Location was not specified
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7108172@advancements.scouting.org
DTSTAMP:20260823T214103Z
CREATED:20260818T192456Z
ORGANIZER:Nicolas Sfeir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260912T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260912T130000
SUMMARY:Kayaking Merit Badge
DESCRIPTION:Howdy Scouts\,\nWe have scheduled our Kayaking Merit Badge activities with Austin Paddleboard and Kayak (APK) on 9/12/26 at 11AM.\nWhat to bring: sunscreen\, hat\, water shoes (optional)\, and a water bottle.\nAPK will provide the kayaks\, paddles\, and life vests. We got a discounted rate of $25 per person\, payable upon arrival at APK.\nYou must have passed the swim test to participate in this event.\nAdults: we will need volunteers on kayaks to support all the different required activities. Feel free to reach out with any questions or concerns.\nYIS\,Nico Sfeir702-604-1178
