SUMMARY:Grayson Dehner Eagle Project
DESCRIPTION:Hi Troop 52!Â I am working toward completing my Eagle Scout rank and would appreciate your help with my Eagle Scout Service Project on Saturday\, August 29 from 8:00 AM to approximately 1:00 PM at Lakeway Airpark.Â For my project\, I will be leading volunteers in building and installing two new picnic tables at Lakeway Airpark. The new tables will provide a better place for pilots\, airport visitors\, families\, and members of the community to gather\, watch airplanes\, and enjoy the airpark\, including during the airpark's monthly community events.Â What We'll Be DoingWe'll divide into teams to work on different parts of the project\, including:Assembling the picnic tablesDrilling and installing hardwareSanding and finishingMoving and organizing materialsRemoving the old tablesInstalling and inspecting the completed tablesCleanupÂ No woodworking experience is necessary. I'll have the materials prepared and will organize everyone into teams and provide instructions before we begin.Â What to Wear &amp; BringÂ Please wear closed-toe shoes and work clothes that can get dirty. Bring safety glasses\, work gloves\, sunscreen\, a hat\, and a water bottle if you have them.Â We'll start with a safety briefing and team assignments at 8:00 AM\, so please try to arrive on time.Â Whether you can stay for the entire project or just part of the morning\, I would really appreciate your help. Please RSVP through Scoutbook so I can plan the work teams\, materials\, food\, and drinks.Â Thank you for supporting my Eagle Scout project and helping make a lasting improvement to Lakeway Airpark!Â Yours in Scouting\,Â Grayson Dehner\n Life Scout\, Troop 52
